From: Tessel <noreply@nobaraproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tile into a grid and resize tiles live

Turning tiling on attached every open window before any tile had a size,
so each split was made across the whole (wide) screen and the windows
ended up as one row of narrow, full-height columns. Measure the layout
before each split, and when several windows arrive at once split the
largest tile, which gives a grid. A window opened later splits the focused
tile, or the largest one when the focused tile is less than half its size.

Resizing a tile with the mouse let the window cover its neighbours until
the button was released, and then moved the nearest divider of the right
orientation, which was not always the one under the dragged edge. Move the
divider under the dragged edge while the pointer moves, so the neighbours
follow.

With a gap between tiles, the gap is a handle: hovering it shows a resize
cursor and dragging it with the left button moves that divider.
---
